date
Usage: date [OPTIONS] [+FMT] [[-s] TIME]

Show or set the current date and time.

	-u		Work in UTC, not local
	[-s] TIME	Set time to TIME
	-d TIME		Display TIME, not 'now'
	-D FMT		FMT (strptime format) for -s/-d TIME conversion
	-r FILE		Display last modification time of FILE
	-R		Output RFC-2822 date
	-I[SPEC]	Output ISO-8601 date
			SPEC=date (default), hours, minutes, seconds or ns

Recognized TIME formats:
	@seconds_since_1970
	hh:mm[:ss]
	[YYYY.]MM.DD-hh:mm[:ss]
	YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm[:ss]
	[[[[[YY]YY]MM]DD]hh]mm[.ss]
	'date TIME' form accepts MMDDhhmm[[YY]YY][.ss] instead

+FMT fields:
	%Y	4-digit year
	%m	Month (01-12)
	%d	Day of month (01-31)
	%H	Hour, 24h (00-23)
	%M	Minute (00-59)
	%S	Second (00-59)
	%s	Seconds since 1970 (epoch)
	%F	Same as %Y-%m-%d
